The two <dot products> are $\mathbf a\cdot\mathbf b=2-1-6=-5$ and $\mathbf b\cdot\mathbf c=-1-3=-4$. Therefore
$$
\boxed{(\mathbf a\cdot\mathbf b)\mathbf c+\mathbf a(\mathbf b\cdot\mathbf c)
=-5(0,1,-1)-4(1,1,-2)=(-4,-9,13)}.
$$

= b
{parent=1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The <cross product> is $\mathbf a\times\mathbf b=(1,-7,-3)$. Taking its <dot product> with $\mathbf c$ gives the <scalar triple product>
$$
\boxed{(\mathbf a\times\mathbf b)\cdot\mathbf c=-7+3=-4}.
$$

