= Solution
{parent=a}

For <independent events> from fair dice, the <probability> of a six on each roll is $1/6$. Multiplication gives
$$
\boxed{P(\text{all sixes})=(1/6)^3=\frac1{216}}.
$$

= b
{parent=10}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The <complement of an event> here is that all three dice avoid six, with <probability> $(5/6)^3$. Therefore
$$
\boxed{P(\text{at least one six})=1-(5/6)^3=\frac{91}{216}}.
$$

= 11
{parent=Paper 2}
